  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring residential health care facilities and adult homes to advise current and prospective residents of the financial condition of the facility",
    "basePrintNo": "S766",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S766-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 32,
       "fullName": "Luis R. Sepúlveda",
       "imgName": "493_Luis_Sepulveda.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1142,
       "sessionMemberId": 1140,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "SEPULVEDA"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §460-d, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S766\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring\nresidential health care facilities and adult homes to advise current\nand prospective residents of the financial condition of the facility\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nRequires the Department of Health to provide written notification to\nresidential health care facilities when a temporary operator has been\nappointed.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill shall provide written notification to residents of all adult\nhomes, enriched housing programs, residences for adults and assisted\nprograms when a temporary operator has been appointed.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nTo provide patients and prospective patients with full disclosure\nabout the current financial status of the nursing home facility or\nmanaged residential community so that patients can make an informed\ndecision about admission.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2013-14: S4068 - Died in Finance (Passed Assembly)\n2015-16: S3444 - Died in Finance (Passed Assembly)\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
